  "body": "## What happens\n\n`tilt()` writes `G43.4 H<n>` for each section that states an A word. When such a section ends with all rotaries at zero, `endPreamble` sets `tcpmOn = false` and writes no `G49`. Then `uprightAtEnd()` returns false, because no rotary is held away from zero. `onClose` writes `G91 G28 Z0` and `G28 X0 Y0` while tool centre point control is still active on the control.\n\nThe FANUC 30i manual gives a list of the G codes that are permitted in G43.4 mode. A reference return is not in it, so the control stops with an alarm. The \"Go home\" after-action already writes `G49` first (the post's comment at `fanuc.cps:863-865` says why), but the program end does not.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe program end writes `G49` before the reference return when G43.4 is active.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:368-373`: `tilt()` arms G43.4.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:902`: `tcpmOn = false` with no `G49`.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:790-799`: `uprightAtEnd()` writes `G49` only when a rotary is held.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:1387-1393`: `onClose`.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:866`: the \"Go home\" path writes `G49` first.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:566-570`, `:848-856`, `:975`, `:1497`: the same in the Doosan DNM post.\n- FANUC Series 30i operator's manual B-63944EN/02, p. 699 and p. 737.\n\nWorkaround: set the last tilted operation to \"Go home\".\n\nFound by the post audit against the Fanuc manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n- After a G43.4 section, both posts write `G49` before the program-end retract.\n- A golden of a tilted section that ends at A0 pins the order.\n",
